# Single read-only index submodule.
#
# 2026-08-18: every cloud-* repo embeds ONLY `cloud` — the fleet index,
# formerly cloud-master. https:// rather than git@ makes it read-only in
# practice: the index is consumed here, never pushed from here.
#
# This does NOT reintroduce the 2026-08-11 problem recorded below. That
# removal was about repos indexing each OTHER as submodules. `cloud` declares
# no submodules of its own — it indexes the fleet with committed RELATIVE
# symlinks, which simply dangle inside a submodule checkout and cost nothing.
# So there is no cloud -> cloud-master -> cloud recursion, and `cloud` is
# public, so `submodule update --init` works without credentials.
#
# unix-ship-repo-workflow-engine.sh reconciles declaratively against this
# file: declared-but-unregistered gets `git submodule add`, registered-but-
# undeclared gets `git rm --cached`. Deleting this section removes it again.
#
# --- 2026-08-11 (kept for context) -------------------------------------
# The five submodules here (I_cloud-data, II_tools, III_front-data,
# IV_cloud-configs, V_front-configs) were removed. They were pure index
# duplication of clones that already exist as siblings in ~/git; nothing read
# through them at runtime and no workflow checked them out. Add repos to the
# index registry (cloud/repos.json), not here.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------

[submodule "cloud"]
	path = cloud
	url = https://github.com/diegonmarcos/cloud.git
	shallow = true
	ignore = all
